# Norton 16H 490 cc motorcycle with sidecar, 1937-1945.
#
# The WD Norton 16H: the 490 cc side-valve single, the standard British
# military despatch machine of the Second World War, here in combination
# form with a sidecar. The 16H was built mostly as a solo machine; the
# standard WD outfit was the Big Four, which is already in the tree. No
# period photograph of a 16H with sidecar was found, so the machine is the
# 16H the pack photographs and the chair is a period-correct combination
# recorded as such.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norton_16H
#
# Dimensions: solo machine 2.172 x 0.762 x 0.991 m on a 1.372 m wheelbase
# (RM Sotheby's 1940 car); a second published set gives 2.108 x 0.737 x
# 1.041 m. Outfit width is not published; the model's chair width is a
# period estimate recorded in the master.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a museum right-side elevation of a WD 16H
# (solo); images 2-4 are period despatch-rider and comparable-outfit
# photographs, each labelled as such in the notes.
#
# Colours: WD finish, Army Service Green/khaki with dull chrome and a white
# census number. One colourway. Weight 80, provisional.
#
# Speed 70 km/h. Comfort 25/338, below the Mini's 40/390: an open chair with
# an exposed rider. Classes 0,1.
# Dates are road presence: 1937 intro, retires 1958.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/norton-16h-combo.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/norton-16h-combo.dae. References:
# citycars/references/norton-16h-combo/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons and
# period photographs).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no confirmed period photograph of an exact 16H
# combination. The chair and its mounts are estimates based on comparable Norton
# outfits, and the chair wheel hubs and screen are simplified. Stage B lateral
# shift +0.3179 pak units, so that the motorcycle rather than the combined
# bounding box sits at the tile centre; the chair is on the nearside.


obj=citycar
name=Norton16HCombo(KhakiGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=80
intro_year=1937
intro_month=1
retire_year=1958
retire_month=6
speed=70
length=2
class=0,1
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=25
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=338

